{"id": "077e9b5e5b803672:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:110cac1c5b5d06c4", "source_id": "077e9b5e5b803672", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/additional-resources/retirement-toolkit/employer-sponsored-plans/traditional-and-roth-401k-plans", "topic": "401(k) Plans", "subtopic": "Tax-Deferred Retirement Savings", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "You pay the taxes on contributions and earnings when the savings are withdrawn.", "question": "Misconception: Money in a traditional 401(k) is never taxed. What is the correction?", "answer": "Taxes on traditional 401(k) contributions and investment earnings are deferred, not eliminated. You pay the taxes when the savings are withdrawn.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1179, "output_tokens": 184}}
{"id": "077e9b5e5b803672:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:65fe4922da2f8097", "source_id": "077e9b5e5b803672", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/additional-resources/retirement-toolkit/employer-sponsored-plans/traditional-and-roth-401k-plans", "topic": "401(k) Plans", "subtopic": "401(k) Investment Options", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A 401(k) plan is an employer-sponsored retirement plan that gives employees a choice of investment options, often various mutual funds. A popular type of fund in 401(k) plans is called a target date fund.", "question": null, "answer": "A 401(k) plan lets employees choose among investment options, which often include various mutual funds. One popular type is a target date fund. Some options held within retirement accounts may be collective investment trusts (CITs), which are not regulated by the SEC, so it is useful to know what type of investment an option represents.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1180, "output_tokens": 229}}
{"id": "077e9b5e5b803672:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:65fe4922da2f8097", "source_id": "077e9b5e5b803672", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/additional-resources/retirement-toolkit/employer-sponsored-plans/traditional-and-roth-401k-plans", "topic": "401(k) Plans", "subtopic": "401(k) Investment Options", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A 401(k) plan is an employer-sponsored retirement plan that gives employees a choice of investment options, often various mutual funds.", "question": "What kinds of investment options might an employee find in a 401(k) plan?", "answer": "A 401(k) plan may offer a choice of investments, often including various mutual funds. Target date funds are also a popular type of fund in 401(k) plans.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1180, "output_tokens": 221}}
{"id": "077e9b5e5b803672:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:65fe4922da2f8097", "source_id": "077e9b5e5b803672", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/additional-resources/retirement-toolkit/employer-sponsored-plans/traditional-and-roth-401k-plans", "topic": "401(k) Plans", "subtopic": "401(k) Investment Options", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "A 401(k) plan is an employer-sponsored retirement plan that gives employees a choice of investment options, often various mutual funds.", "question": "Misconception: A 401(k) offers only one investment option, so employees cannot choose how their money is invested.", "answer": "A 401(k) gives employees a choice of investment options, often including various mutual funds. Target date funds are also a popular type of fund in 401(k) plans.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1180, "output_tokens": 278}}
